          "code": "import numpy as np\nfrom scipy.spatial.distance import cdist\nfrom sklearn.metrics import silhouette_score\n\nrng = np.random.default_rng(2021)\n\n# 3 Klaster di R^6 dengan varians sangat berbeda (rapat vs sedang vs renggang)\nn_per = 40\nX1 = rng.normal(loc=[0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0], scale=0.25, size=(n_per, 6))\nX2 = rng.normal(loc=[5, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0], scale=0.80, size=(n_per, 6))\nX3 = rng.normal(loc=[2, 6, 0, 0, 0, 0], scale=2.20, size=(n_per, 6))\nX = np.vstack([X1, X2, X3])\nlabels = np.repeat([0, 1, 2], n_per)\nn = X.shape[0]\n\n# 1) Pencarian Biner Kalibrasi sigma_i untuk Target Perplexity = 15.0\nD2 = cdist(X, X, metric=\"sqeuclidean\")\ntarget_perp = 15.0\ntarget_H = np.log(target_perp)\nP_cond = np.zeros((n, n))\nsigmas = np.zeros(n)\n\nfor i in range(n):\n    beta_lo, beta_hi, beta = 1e-6, 1e6, 1.0\n    di = np.delete(D2[i], i)\n    for _ in range(50):\n        logits = -di * beta\n        logits -= np.max(logits)\n        w = np.exp(logits)\n        p = w / np.sum(w)\n        H = -float(np.sum(p * np.log(np.maximum(p, 1e-12))))\n        if abs(H - target_H) < 1e-5:\n            break\n        if H > target_H:\n            beta_lo = beta\n            beta = beta * 2.0 if beta_hi >= 1e5 else 0.5 * (beta + beta_hi)\n        else:\n            beta_hi = beta\n            beta = beta * 0.5 if beta_lo <= 1e-5 else 0.5 * (beta + beta_lo)\n    sigmas[i] = 1.0 / np.sqrt(2.0 * beta)\n    idx_other = np.arange(n) != i\n    P_cond[i, idx_other] = p\n\nP = (P_cond + P_cond.T) / (2.0 * n)\nP = np.maximum(P, 1e-12)\n\n# Inisialisasi PCA deterministik skala kecil\nXc = X - X.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n_, _, Vt = np.linalg.svd(Xc, full_matrices=False)\nY_init = (Xc @ Vt[:2].T)\nY_init = Y_init / (np.std(Y_init[:, 0]) + 1e-12) * 0.05\n\n# 2) Bandingkan Optimasi Symmetric Gaussian SNE vs Student-t t-SNE (Early Exaggeration + Momentum)\ndef run_sne(P_mat: np.ndarray, Y0: np.ndarray, kernel: str, n_iter: int = 200, lr: float = 15.0):\n    Y = Y0.copy()\n    vel = np.zeros_like(Y)\n    for it in range(n_iter):\n        P_eff = P_mat * 4.0 if it < 60 else P_mat\n        Dy2 = cdist(Y, Y, metric=\"sqeuclidean\")\n        if kernel == \"student_t\":\n            W = 1.0 / (1.0 + Dy2)\n            np.fill_diagonal(W, 0.0)\n            Q = np.maximum(W / np.sum(W), 1e-12)\n            stiff = (P_eff - Q) * W\n        else:  # Gaussian SNE klasik -> rawan crowding! (log-sum-exp stabil agar bebas underflow)\n            neg_d = -Dy2\n            np.fill_diagonal(neg_d, -np.inf)\n            shift = float(np.max(neg_d))\n            W = np.exp(neg_d - shift)\n            np.fill_diagonal(W, 0.0)\n            Q = np.maximum(W / np.sum(W), 1e-12)\n            stiff = (P_eff - Q)\n        # Gradien: dC/dy_i = 4 * sum_j stiff_ij * (y_i - y_j)\n        grad = 4.0 * (np.sum(stiff, axis=1, keepdims=True) * Y - stiff @ Y)\n        grad = np.clip(grad, -2.0, 2.0)\n        mom = 0.5 if it < 60 else 0.8\n        vel = mom * vel - lr * grad\n        Y += vel\n        Y -= Y.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n    Dy2 = cdist(Y, Y, metric=\"sqeuclidean\")\n    if kernel == \"student_t\":\n        W = 1.0 / (1.0 + Dy2)\n    else:\n        neg_d = -Dy2\n        np.fill_diagonal(neg_d, -np.inf)\n        W = np.exp(neg_d - float(np.max(neg_d)))\n    np.fill_diagonal(W, 0.0)\n    Q = np.maximum(W / np.sum(W), 1e-12)\n    kl = float(np.sum(P_mat * np.log(P_mat / Q)))\n    return Y, kl\n\nY_gauss, kl_gauss = run_sne(P, Y_init, kernel=\"gaussian\")\nY_tsne, kl_tsne = run_sne(P, Y_init, kernel=\"student_t\")\n\ndef dynamic_range_ratio(Y: np.ndarray) -> float:\n    d = cdist(Y, Y, metric=\"euclidean\")\n    tri = d[np.triu_indices(len(Y), k=1)]\n    return float(np.percentile(tri, 90) / max(np.percentile(tri, 10), 1e-9))\n\nprint(\"=== 1. Kalibrasi Adaptif sigma_i (Target Perplexity=15.0) ===\")\nfor c, name in enumerate([\"Klaster 0 (sigma asli=0.25)\", \"Klaster 1 (sigma asli=0.80)\", \"Klaster 2 (sigma asli=2.20)\"]):\n    print(f\"  {name} -> Mean sigma_i terkalibrasi = {sigmas[labels == c].mean():.4f}\")\n\nprint(\"\\n=== 2. Crowding Problem: Symmetric Gaussian SNE vs Student-t t-SNE (From Scratch) ===\")\nprint(f\"Gaussian SNE  | Final KL = {kl_gauss:.4f} | Silhouette = {silhouette_score(Y_gauss, labels):.4f} | Rasio Jarak p90/p10 = {dynamic_range_ratio(Y_gauss):.2f}\")\nprint(f\"Student-t SNE | Final KL = {kl_tsne:.4f} | Silhouette = {silhouette_score(Y_tsne, labels):.4f} | Rasio Jarak p90/p10 = {dynamic_range_ratio(Y_tsne):.2f}\")",
          "expectedOutput": "=== 1. Kalibrasi Adaptif sigma_i (Target Perplexity=15.0) ===\n  Klaster 0 (sigma asli=0.25) -> Mean sigma_i terkalibrasi = 0.2681\n  Klaster 1 (sigma asli=0.80) -> Mean sigma_i terkalibrasi = 0.8644\n  Klaster 2 (sigma asli=2.20) -> Mean sigma_i terkalibrasi = 2.0044\n\n=== 2. Crowding Problem: Symmetric Gaussian SNE vs Student-t t-SNE (From Scratch) ===\nGaussian SNE  | Final KL = 0.5547 | Silhouette = 0.5282 | Rasio Jarak p90/p10 = 6.16\nStudent-t SNE | Final KL = 0.4606 | Silhouette = 0.6357 | Rasio Jarak p90/p10 = 6.03",
