          "solution": "```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef calibrate_perplexity_and_tail_ratio(sq_dists_dense, sq_dists_sparse, target_perp: float = 8.0, d_mid: float = 3.0) -> tuple[float, float, float, float]:\n    def solve_sigma(sq_d):\n        sq_d = np.asarray(sq_d, dtype=float)\n        target_H = np.log(target_perp)\n        lo, hi, beta = 1e-6, 1e6, 1.0\n        for _ in range(60):\n            logits = -sq_d * beta\n            logits -= np.max(logits)\n            w = np.exp(logits)\n            p = w / np.sum(w)\n            H = -float(np.sum(p * np.log(np.maximum(p, 1e-12))))\n            if abs(H - target_H) < 1e-7:\n                break\n            if H > target_H:\n                lo = beta\n                beta = beta * 2.0 if hi >= 1e5 else 0.5 * (beta + hi)\n            else:\n                hi = beta\n                beta = beta * 0.5 if lo <= 1e-5 else 0.5 * (beta + lo)\n        return float(1.0 / np.sqrt(2.0 * beta)), float(np.exp(H))\n    sig_d, perp_d = solve_sigma(sq_dists_dense)\n    sig_s, _ = solve_sigma(sq_dists_sparse)\n    tail_ratio = float((1.0 / (1.0 + d_mid ** 2)) / np.exp(-(d_mid ** 2)))\n    return (round(sig_d, 4), round(sig_s, 4), round(perp_d, 4), round(tail_ratio, 2))\n```"
